 - 2026-06-25: PHASE A1 (ARC NORTH STAR; PRIMARY; HEADLINE) -- REPLACE THE 0.12-ACCURATE FREE-FORM ENGINE WITH THE EXISTING STRUCTURED ProductWorldModel. The 2026-06-25 end-to-end measurement proved the free-form LLM engine induction is the binding wall: lp85's L1 world model reproduced only 0.12 of observed transitions (world_model_accuracy_below_threshold) -- the model writes a placeholder engine. A structured engine with the EXACT (grid,action,data)->next_grid signature ALREADY EXISTS (ProductWorldModel.engine, arc_executable_world_model.py:427) fed by induce_programmatic_object_experts (:331). Build a load_engine adapter that returns (ProductWorldModel(induced experts).engine, goal) and wire it (env-gated CARNOT_ARC_STRUCTURED_ENGINE=1) into the live level_up_reinduction call site (arc_competition_agent.py:2494, in place of e3.load_engine). NON-DEGENERACY GATE INLINE: PROVE the structured engine actually changes cells (engine output differs from the input grid on >0 actions) BEFORE any accuracy claim. WIN: the structured engine's held-out transition accuracy on >=1 real game (lp85/sc25/m0r0) beats the free-form 0.12 by a wide margin (target >=0.5) AND the L2 reinduction runs on it without proposer_failed OR a multi-level probe reaches L2 offline-reproduced. verifier_is_oracle:false. live_agent_self_discovery. retire_if_same_verdict. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_structured_engine_no_improvement_null; results/experiment_4749_structured_engine_vs_freeform.json
 - 2026-06-26: PHASE A2 (ARC NORTH STAR; PRIMARY) -- FIX THE STRUCTURAL-ALIGNMENT GOAL DETECTOR over-segmentation that nulled exp4712. The perception-grounded structural-alignment goal pipeline already exists end-to-end (arc_value_learner.py detect_marker_pair_shape_alignment:752 + structural_alignment_goal_candidate:845, wired at arc_competition_agent.py:2480-2504) but exp4712 nulled (l2_perception_goal_no_deepening_residual_alignment_under_determined): on lp85's real post-L1 frame the detector returns goal_count=42 (every solid-2x2 same-color component classified a goal sprite), aligned_piece_count=0 -> the piece->sprite pairing is under-determined -> the goal is never satisfiable. Resolve the segmentation/pairing (_is_solid_2x2_component:716 + _corner_marker_pieces:724 over-segment) so is_level_complete is SATISFIABLE on a reachable grid AND plan_reaches_goal. WIN: goal_predicate_satisfiable =True AND lp85 reaches L2 offline-reproduced. SANCTIONED FALLBACK if it still nulls: the MULTI-EXEMPLAR variant (bank >=2 L1-completion exemplars), NOT the retired CNN driver. verifier_is_oracle:false. live_agent_self_discovery. retire_if_same_verdict. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete_detector_fixed_but_no_bank_no_reachable_plan; results/experiment_4750_structural_alignment_detector_fix.json
 - 2026-06-26: PHASE A3 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY; LEVEL-UP ATTEMPT GUARANTEE + SELF-PLAY EVERY MILESTONE) -- run the standing self-play loop (scripts/arc_loop_solve.py) to BANK +1 NEW reproducible level on a CLEAN game NOT deepened in recent milestones (PREFER a first-contact L1->L2 of an UNSOLVED public game from re86/s5i5/g50t/lf52/bp35/sb26, alternatives a +1 deeper level on a shallow-solved game) AND train+checkpoint the learned verifier on pos/neg traces. Gate: offline_reproduced a NEW level -> reproducible_total_levels grows by >=1. verifier_is_oracle:false. live_agent_self_discovery. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: sk48_L2_offline_reproduced; results/experiment_4751_levelup_selfplay.json
+- 2026-06-26: PHASE A4 (ARC NORTH STAR; SCORE -- held-out first-win readiness lane) -- re-measure the held-out first-win rate + CI + multi-level deepen rate over the held-out public-game proxy, ROBUST to the codex 4800s cap by reusing the exp4729 checkpoint/resume soft-budget (EXP4729_SOFT_BUDGET_S=4200, ~600s under the cap). Report the leaderboard-readiness delta vs the prior milestone; submission stays operator-only. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: held_out_first_win_flat_no_leaderboard_change; results/experiment_4752_held_out_first_win_readiness.json
